{
  "_comment": "DESIGN.md §7. Four complete rosters, six units each, every one of them covering all four damage types (§6.1). A Mark II on every line, a Mark III on ten of them (§7.3). EVERY UNIT HAS AN ABILITY: the signature one from Mark I, its numbers rising with the mark (`rank`), and a second one unlocked by the top of its ladder - which for a three-mark line is an ability that spends energy. `abilities.json` holds all of them; a builder is its six units plus what those abilities do together. Pricing aims at ~1.6x cost for ~2.2x value so going tall beats going wide, but needs board presence you already paid for. RUNG is which of the six lines a unit belongs to, 1 (cheapest) to 6 (dearest), and is the power ladder the price bands are set against. MARK is how far up its own upgrade chain it is - I, II, III - and upgrading happens in place. The two words used to share one field called `tier`, which meant both and read as neither. DESIGN CHANGE from §5.2: moveSpeed is how fast a unit advances when nothing is in range; 0 pins it in place. `range` is reach measured EDGE TO EDGE, so a melee value near zero means walking up and touching rather than stopping a body-width short. `bodyRadius` is both collision and drawn size. All placeholders.",
  "builders": [
    {
      "id": "ironvow",
      "name": "Ironvow",
      "complete": true,
      "_roster": "Ironvow: an order under oath, and the roster that reads most like a LINE. Shields, taunts and answered blows - Oathwall makes itself the target, Pledge is worth more with a Pledge beside it, Vigil hands out wards, and Judgement and Sanction are what the line is protecting. Defence and support first; its damage comes from being allowed to stand still."
    },
    {
      "id": "pyre",
      "name": "Pyre",
      "complete": true,
      "_roster": "Pyre: heat that builds. Almost everything it owns applies `burning` or is paid extra for hitting something already alight, and the longer a Pyre unit fires the faster it fires. It dies quickly and does not care - Slagmaw burns whatever kills it and Wickling and Scoria are gone before the wave is. Offence first, with no answer to being outlasted."
    },
    {
      "id": "thornweald",
      "name": "Thornweald",
      "complete": true,
      "_roster": "Thornweald: slow strangulation. Roots and rot rather than damage - Rootbite grinds a wave to a walk, Bloomspread and Wilt leave it blighted and unable to heal, and Heartwood and Underweb mean its own line is still standing when the wave is not. Control and support, and the only roster that repairs itself."
    },
    {
      "id": "gloomtide",
      "name": "Gloomtide",
      "complete": true,
      "_roster": "Gloomtide: pressure and cold. It soaks a wave and then charges it for being wet - Snarekelp and Sleetfall apply `soaked`, and Torrential, Undertow, Hailburst and Drownward all pay extra for it. Long reach, slow swings, and Murmur keeping time. Control and artillery, weak to anything that reaches it."
    }
  ],
